"This week Venn is riding the southern Flats, a few hours from where Nala woke."
"Venn heard the Flats ring wrong the afternoon Nala came, a sharp chime with no wind, and turned north."
"Venn's binding paper is a facsimile contract: it holds only if its signer signs it freely."
"Venn and the Ashfur band are at feud: he took a bengai cub three summers ago and Oru wants him dead."
"Venn sells the best of what he takes to an eastern buyer through Dask, off the Orrow books."
